{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f07e39d99b57bc5b02", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Ray Optics - Test 6", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb67"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb1c", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca57", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5677"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b4f"], "question": {"text": "<p>A monochromatic light wave with wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in air enters another medium. If the angle of incidence and angle of refraction at the interface are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> respectively, then the wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;of the refracted wave are:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "590a57", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca58"}, {"id": "907e29", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca59"}, {"id": "fcba31", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca5a"}, {"id": "296546", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca5b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca5c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4707"], "question": {"text": "<p>Curved surfaces of a plano-convex lens of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and a plano-concave lens of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> have equal radius of curvature as shown in figure. Find the ratio of radius of curvature to the focal length of the combined lenses</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff722c22a-76a3-43c1-8aae-b9b843aad7e5-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 104px; height: 179px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "fbc0d5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca5d"}, {"id": "f85fb5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca5e"}, {"id": "537a9f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca5f"}, {"id": "dfca67", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca60"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca61", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f39"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4efc"], "question": {"text": "When an object is placed 40 cm away from a spherical mirror an image of magnification $\\frac{1}{2}$ is produced. To obtain an image with magnification of $\\frac{1}{3}$, the object is to be moved :"}, "options": [{"id": "ee0b9c", "text": "40 cm away from the mirror.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca62"}, {"id": "38107c", "text": "80 cm away from the mirror.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca63"}, {"id": "605d2f", "text": "20 cm towards the mirror.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca64"}, {"id": "8e9bf5", "text": "20 cm away from the mirror.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca65"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca66", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c2"], "question": {"text": "A convex lens of focal length <math><mn>20</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> produces images of the same magnification 2 when an object is kept at two distances <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> from the lens. The ratio of <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "a8237f", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca67"}, {"id": "694af0", "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca68"}, {"id": "d7974c", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca69"}, {"id": "39f7ff", "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca6a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca6b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5677"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b4f"], "question": {"text": "The critical angle for a denser-rarer interface is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.&nbsp;The speed of light in rarer medium is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The speed of light in the denser medium is:"}, "options": [{"id": "397b63", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca6c"}, {"id": "54bd0c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca6d"}, {"id": "15d786", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca6e"}, {"id": "d767db", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca6f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca70", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b30"], "question": {"text": "The power of a lens (biconvex) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in particular medium. Refractive index of the lens is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and radii of curvature are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively. The refractive index of surrounding medium:"}, "options": [{"id": "17eb40", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca71"}, {"id": "baea29", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca72"}, {"id": "be0a59", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca73"}, {"id": "8a6ff2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca74"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca75", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5677"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b4f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as <strong>Assertion A</strong> and the other is labelled as <strong>Reason R</strong></p><p><strong>Assertion A:</strong> The phase difference of two light waves change if they travel through different media having same thickness, but different indices of&nbsp; refraction.</p><p><strong>Reason R:</strong> The wavelengths of waves are different in different media.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "546682", "text": "Both <strong>A</strong> and <strong>R</strong> are correct but <strong>R</strong> is NOT the correct explanation of <strong>A</strong>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca76"}, {"id": "168568", "text": "<strong>A</strong> is not correct but <strong>R</strong> is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca77"}, {"id": "04b032", "text": "<strong>A</strong> is correct but <strong>R</strong> is not correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca78"}, {"id": "afb7f5", "text": "Both <strong>A</strong> and <strong>R</strong> are correct and <strong>R</strong> is the correct explanation of <strong>A</strong>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca79"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca7a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa38e"], "question": {"text": "Given a thin convex lens (refractive index $\\mu_2$ ), kept in a liquid (refractive index $\\mu_1, \\mu_1 \\lt \\mu_2$ ) having radii of curvatures $\\left|R_1\\right|$ and $\\left|R_2\\right|$. Its second surface is silver polished. Where should an object be placed on the optic axis so that a real and inverted image is formed at the same place?"}, "options": [{"id": "e41a58", "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right| \\cdot\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}{\\mu_2\\left(\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|+\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|\\right)-\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca7b"}, {"id": "6d4330", "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right| \\cdot\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}{\\mu_2\\left(\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|+\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|\\right)-\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca7c"}, {"id": "2f568f", "text": "$\\frac{\\left(\\mu_2+\\mu_1\\right)\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|}{\\left(\\mu_2-\\mu_1\\right)}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca7d"}, {"id": "e455a4", "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_1\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right| \\cdot\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}{\\mu_2\\left(2\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right|+\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|\\right)-\\mu_1 \\sqrt{\\left|\\mathrm{R}_1\\right| \\cdot\\left|\\mathrm{R}_2\\right|}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca7e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca7f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9250"], "question": {"text": "An object is at a distance of $20 \\mathrm{~m}$ from a convex lens of focal length $0.3 \\mathrm{~m}$. The lens forms an image of the object. If the object moves away from the lens at a speed of $5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ the speed and direction of the image will be"}, "options": [{"id": "92febd", "text": "$2.26 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ away from the lens", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca80"}, {"id": "e96f00", "text": "$0.92 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ away from the lens", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca81"}, {"id": "80dc25", "text": "$3.22 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ towards the lens", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca82"}, {"id": "a9597d", "text": "$1.16 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ towards the lens", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca83"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca84", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["6162fb4c6ed13040ec84d408"], "question": {"text": "A convex lens of focal length 30 cm is placed in contact with a concave lens of focal length 20 cm. An object is placed at 20 cm to the left of this lens system. The distance of the image from the lens in cm is ________"}, "options": [{"id": "aba6c6", "text": "30", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca85"}, {"id": "8a1eb9", "text": "45", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca86"}, {"id": "023c85", "text": "$\\frac{60}{7}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca87"}, {"id": "5b7f7c", "text": "15", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca88"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca89", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["6162fb4c6ed13040ec84d40f"], "question": {"text": "A convex lens is put <math><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math> from a light source and it makes a sharp image on a screen, kept <math><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math> from the lens. Now a glass block (refractive index 1.5) of <math><mn>1.5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math> thickness is placed in between the light source and the lens. To get the sharp image again, the screen is shifted by a distance <math><mi>d</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then <math><mi>d</mi></math> is:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ftiiearzpuvowsfzcnzaxwlczobxkhonljkbwiiycuydzkytezx.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "932c21", "text": "<math><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca8a"}, {"id": "ad1125", "text": "<math><mn>0.55</mn><mi> </mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>  away from the lens", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca8b"}, {"id": "970083", "text": "<math><mn>0.55</mn><mi> </mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>  towards the lens", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca8c"}, {"id": "5d7da0", "text": "<math><mn>1.1</mn><mi> </mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>  away from the lens", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca8d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca8e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["6162fb4c6ed13040ec84d402"], "question": {"text": "Given is a thin convex lens of glass (refractive index $\\mu$ ) and each side having radius of curvature $R$. One side is polished for complete reflection. At what distance from the lens, an object be placed on the optic axis so that the image gets formed on the object itself ?"}, "options": [{"id": "d99d1c", "text": "$\\mathrm{R} / \\mu$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca8f"}, {"id": "2b4a7c", "text": "$R /(2 \\mu-3)$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca90"}, {"id": "d766b7", "text": "$\\mu R$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca91"}, {"id": "f97b06", "text": "$\\mathrm{R} /(2 \\mu-1)$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca92"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca93", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f925a"], "question": {"text": "When a beam of white light is allowed to pass through convex lens parallel to principal axis, the different colours of light converge at different point on the principle axis after refraction. This is called :"}, "options": [{"id": "5edbe6", "text": "Scattering", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca94"}, {"id": "9d69b3", "text": "Chromatic aberration&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca95"}, {"id": "e9e323", "text": "Spherical aberration", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca96"}, {"id": "9ba1ab", "text": "Polarisation", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca97"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca98", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["617aa9daef3fe65ad8e829f9"], "question": {"text": "Let u and \\(v\\) be the distances of the object and the image from a lens of focal length \\(f\\). The correct graphical representation of \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(v\\) for a convex lens when \\(|\\mathbf{u}|\\gt f\\), is"}, "options": [{"id": "2e6e30", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5L9gzDtxNqLAEbw69lMB8_2vpZAAIT9LtoxRb9Ni3M8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca99"}, {"id": "2bee95", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7eL5gOubVl-hwkpKM-rUER8x6ZRZH22wQCiqA6kR2ok.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca9a"}, {"id": "aca5f6", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FnjJbQvSbSqhYLhBWdlFKg9NcR7ieh0M3Xj4ruXrpzlM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca9b"}, {"id": "a46025", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fl2PDBjUjKljwkuUfpnJ-Cal6NXVFjRt4N7cUtdo7MP4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca9c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca9d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4707"], "question": {"text": "The position of the image formed by the combination of lenses is :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FwJ-cPn8WsfeX9ljhXOv8E9_XoTA3QA_i05nVAtrERGA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "831f60", "text": "$15 \\mathrm{~cm}$ (right of second lens)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca9e"}, {"id": "13b2db", "text": "$30 \\mathrm{~cm}$ (left of third lens)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891ca9f"}, {"id": "250c12", "text": "$15 \\mathrm{~cm}$ (left of second lens)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa0"}, {"id": "0ef1a8", "text": "$30 \\mathrm{~cm}$ (right of third lens)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c2"], "question": {"text": "An object is placed at the focus of concave lens having focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>.</mo></math> What is the magnification and distance of the image from the optical centre of the lens?"}, "options": [{"id": "a16640", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa3"}, {"id": "3a396d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa4"}, {"id": "7fb9bf", "text": "Very high, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8734;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa5"}, {"id": "08f06e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b30"], "question": {"text": "The refractive index of a converging lens is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. What will be the focal length of this lens if it is placed in a medium of same refractive index ? (Assume the radii of curvature of the faces of lens are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> respectively)"}, "options": [{"id": "5cbc3f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa8"}, {"id": "a8904f", "text": "Infinite", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caa9"}, {"id": "6749b4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caaa"}, {"id": "4be304", "text": "Zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caab"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caac", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa38e"], "question": {"text": "Formation of real image using a biconvex lens is shown below:<br /><br><br /><br><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ficqmczijpkhcccnouixhlakkrksjicssstveasfxvjtohyxgbf.png?alt=media\" /><br /><br><br /><br>If the whole set up is immersed in water without disturbing the object and the screen positions, what will one observe on the screen?"}, "options": [{"id": "8eb51b", "text": "Image disappears", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caad"}, {"id": "0ae445", "text": "Magnified image", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caae"}, {"id": "319639", "text": "Erect real image", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caaf"}, {"id": "5c8396", "text": "No change", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9250"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;meter long scale with least count of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is used to measure the locations of objects on an optical bench. While measuring the focal length of&nbsp;a convex lens, the object pin and the convex lens are placed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> mark and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> mark, respectively. The image of the object pin on the other side of lens coincides with image pin that is kept at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> mark. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> error in the estimation of focal length is:"}, "options": [{"id": "fc376e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab2"}, {"id": "6c889a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>70</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab3"}, {"id": "716792", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab4"}, {"id": "4ede29", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>51</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4707"], "question": {"text": "The following figure represents two biconvex lenses $L_1$ and $L_2$ having focal length $10 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and $15 \\mathrm{~cm}$ respectively. The distance between $L_1 \\& L_2$ is :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FWi-SoTvtuWt7ao_OIb3jjJy2mDygvob8_ZdqMSk08Rk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "937315", "text": "$10 \\mathrm{~cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab7"}, {"id": "57f913", "text": "$35 \\mathrm{~cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab8"}, {"id": "dd3de2", "text": "$25 \\mathrm{~cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cab9"}, {"id": "9aaffc", "text": "$15 \\mathrm{~cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891caba"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:58.641Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:58.641Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb65"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb63", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb47", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b30"], "question": {"text": "Light from a point source in air falls on a spherical glass surface (refractive index, $\\mu=1.5$ and radius of curvature $=50 \\mathrm{~cm}$). The image is formed at a distance of 200 cm from the glass surface inside the glass. The magnitude of distance of the light source from the glass surface is ____ m."}, "options": [{"id": "2a58bc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb48"}, {"id": "6ffe72", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb49"}, {"id": "915172", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb4a"}, {"id": "120e18", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb4b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb4c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c538326"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f925c"], "question": {"text": "The refractive index of a transparent liquid filled in an equilateral hollow prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>. The angle of minimum deviation for the liquid will be _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#176;</mo></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "6043f8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb4d"}, {"id": "357c93", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb4e"}, {"id": "d21819", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb4f"}, {"id": "6ebe77", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb50"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb51", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5677"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b4f"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the given figure, the face <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> of the equilateral prism is immersed in a liquid of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>. For incident angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> at the side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, the refracted light beam just grazes along face <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. The refractive index of the liquid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .<br />(Given refractive index of glass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F40808055-3ef7-4635-82a5-02c7363c3d64-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 167px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c61394", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb52"}, {"id": "e39a98", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb53"}, {"id": "1552fb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb54"}, {"id": "69267e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb55"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb56", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b474f"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b22"], "question": {"text": "An object viewed from a near point distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, using a microscopic lens with magnification <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo></math> gives an unresolved image. A resolved image is observed at infinite distance with a total magnification double the earlier using an eyepiece along with the given lens and a tube of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, if the focal length of the eyepiece is equal to ____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "aa641b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb57"}, {"id": "04d9f5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb58"}, {"id": "97a134", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb59"}, {"id": "15dff3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb5a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb5b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3b"], "concepts": ["6162fb466ed13040ec84d055"], "question": {"text": "<p>Two vertical parallel mirrors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are separated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> cm. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> point object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The distance of the second nearest image behind mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;from the mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F29a386be-8f49-478b-b5df-786741b8b822.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 306px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "49e3ea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb5c"}, {"id": "296e99", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb5d"}, {"id": "ff8d34", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb5e"}, {"id": "ab468c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb5f"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:58.779Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:58.779Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f66c677dc36a891cb66"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:00.679Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:00.960Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analy